;; Leaf functions that run out of the usual registers.
;;
;; Hand-written, and it stays hand-written, though twenty-four values carried
;; round a loop make every function long and regular: test/gen_cases.py does
;; not emit a file of this name, and run_cases.py globs the directory
;; afterwards, so this is run against wasm-interp like every generated case
;; is.
;;
;; What it is for.  A function that makes no call keeps the instance and the
;; memory base in x9 and x10, which leaves x19 and x20 idle, and it has no
;; frame record to keep in x29 and no return address to keep in x30 but the
;; one its ret reads.  The allocator takes all four once the others are gone,
;; and the prologue saves them like any callee-saved pair.  Every function
;; here carries more values round its loop than the other registers hold, so
;; each exercises some of the four, through:
;;
;;   * a plain return, where the epilogue restores x30 before the ret;
;;   * a tail call, where the teardown restores x29 and x30 after the
;;     arguments are in place and before the branch;
;;   * memory reads in the loop, so x10 holds the memory base all along;
;;   * i64 values as well as i32 ones;
